		(property "Description" "RFQ type-B residual-current sensor (fluxgate) around L1-L3 and N - INTERFACE CONTRACT (pcs_spec residual_current_contract, review R2-13; every figure ASSUMED until the part is chosen): type B: AC to >= 2 kHz, pulsating DC and smooth DC residual current (fluxgate), one sensor around every live conductor; trips in firmware from the analog output (the sensor has no trip relay): continuous residual current >= 1250 mA (10 mA per kVA above 30 kVA, 125 kVA) within 0.3 s; sudden changes 30 mA within 0.30 s / 60 mA within 0.15 s / 150 mA within 0.04 s; DC and AC (rms) alike; range +/-2.0 A, +/-(3 % of reading + 3 mA), DC to 1 kHz; resolution <= 6 mA DC / 30 mA AC; OUT analog voltage, 2.50 V +/-1 % at zero residual current, 1.00 V/A +/-3 % (+/-2.0 A in 0.50-4.50 V), DC to >= 2 kHz (-3 dB), >= 0.25 mA into the control board's 10.0k / 13.0k divider, noise <= 3 mA rms equivalent; diagnostic on OUT, no separate pin: an internal fault (fluxgate oscillator stopped, supply out of range, failed self-check) drives OUT to <= 0.25 V or >= 4.75 V within <= 100 ms - outside the 0.50-4.50 V signal band; firmware: sensor fault -> no connection / controlled stop; TEST TEST, 3.3 V CMOS active high, >= 10 kOhm (RCM_TST from GPIO21 through PCS_X, 100k pull-down on the power board): injects 50 mA DC +/-20 % through the test winding, OUT steps by 50 mV +/-20 % within <= 50 ms; used by the start-up self-test and before every connection; supply 5 V +/-5 % from the power board's +5V, <= 50 mA including start-up (the +5V budget's allocation); aperture L1-L3 + N: 4 bars 16 x 4.5 mm on edge with 1 mm sleeves (30.5 x 18 mm, the AC CM choke's fit); the bars are LIVE (V_dc/2 + 375 V x 1.2 against DC-, <= 1050 V DC + the OVC III impulse): bar to sensor electronics through the 1.5 kV rms bar sleeves plus the sensor's own functional insulation, referenced to DC- like the board"
			(at 0 -13.97 0)
			(hide yes)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
			)
		)
